 ## Overview
-Window-Closing Visibility Detection is a conservative visibility culling method designed for perspective navigation within large, tubular datasets, specifically virtual colonoscopy. It solves the problem of efficiently identifying which subvolumes (represented as boxes) lie within the current viewing frustum without performing expensive per-box frustum intersection tests for all candidates. It sets itself apart from its parent, the [Visible Zone Algorithm](9086-visible-zone-algorithm.md), by utilizing a 2D screen-space projection approach that iteratively shrinks a culling window, and from its sibling, the [Approximate Visibility Algorithm](13128-approximate-visibility-algorithm.md), by relying on the geometric "twisted" nature of the colon to guarantee that occlusion is handled via window degeneration rather than approximate distance bounds.
