 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Degenerate ACW:** The algorithm relies on the ACW becoming empty to terminate. If the colon geometry is not sufficiently "twisted" or occluded, the ACW may remain valid for many boxes, reducing culling efficiency.
-*   **Perspective vs. Parallel:** The method is designed for perspective projection. Parallel projection may not benefit from the same occlusion properties. [S1, unofficial]
-*   **Ordering:** Boxes must be processed in an order that respects occlusion (closest to furthest). Incorrect ordering can lead to incorrect visibility determination.
