 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of boxes until the ACW degenerates. Each box requires projection and a constant-time rectangle intersection.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Constant space for the ACW and CCW, plus storage for the box sequence.
-*   **Strengths:** Efficient for tubular structures with significant self-occlusion (like the colon). Avoids expensive 3D frustum intersection tests.
-*   **Limitations:** Relies on the assumption that the structure is "twisted" enough to cause occlusion. Performance degrades if the ACW does not degenerate quickly. Limited to perspective projection as described.
-*   **When to Use:** Interactive navigation in large, tubular volume datasets (e.g., virtual colonoscopy) where occlusion is frequent.
-*   **When Not to Use:** Non-tubular structures, parallel projection, or scenes with low self-occlusion.
