 ## Background
-The Window-Closing Visibility Detection algorithm was developed for virtual colonoscopy applications to enable interactive navigation within large human colon datasets. It was presented in the context of real-time volume rendering, leveraging the twisted nature of the colon to optimize visibility culling. The work was supported by NSF, ONR, NIH, and Mitsubishi Electric grants. [S1, unofficial]
